  11. SERVER ARCHITECTURE (authoritative)
  =====================================================================
  - Server runs map instances; each instance owns a `World` from /shared and steps at 30 Hz with fixed timestep and an accumulator; snapshots to clients at 10 Hz containing only entities within the player's interest radius (use a spatial grid for interest management and collision broad-phase). Deltas: only changed fields; entity ids are stable numbers; protocol messages are typed unions defined in /shared/protocol.ts (client->server: input commands with sequence numbers; server->client: welcome, snapshot/delta, events, chat, errors).
  - Client-side prediction for the own vehicle (replay unacknowledged inputs after each snapshot) and interpolation (~100 ms in the past) for everyone else.
  - All validation server-side: movement speed limits, cooldowns, ammo, range, line of fire, inventory operations, crafting costs, market rules. The client never sends damage, position of hits, loot, or currency.
  - Persistence: periodic and event-based saves per player (on logout, level-up, trade, craft), transactional for currency/item operations; SQLite schema for accounts, profiles, vehicles, items, wallets, transactions, quests, achievements, codex, clans, clan members, clan storage, friends, blocks, chat (limited), reports, market listings, arena ratings, seasons, event log, admin log, bans.
  - Instance manager: capacity, spawning/despawning instances, routing, graceful shutdown with save. Gate/arena instances are created on demand and destroyed when empty.
  - Scheduler: world boss rotation, events, daily/weekly reset (server time), season rollover, arena season rollover, market expiry, faction-war cycle.
  - Observability: structured logs, /health, /metrics (tick time per instance, players, entities, bytes/s), debug overlay in the client.
  - Anti-cheat basics: speed/teleport validation, command rate limit (max N inputs per tick), sequence validation, suspicious-behavior log, bot heuristics (perfectly regular input patterns, 24/7 sessions) flagged in the admin dashboard.
  - Version gate: server rejects clients below a minimum protocol version with a clear "update required" message. Client shows "No connection" with retry; game is online-only.

